+++ b/docs/HARDWARE-CPU-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Production CPU integration closure
+
+This candidate starts at published LightingChips b4f4cee0524ebbfa61a5a9049f27755e05f6492e. It carries the production CPU/MMU/module bridge dependency closure, multiply/divide unit, access-qualified memory transactions, grouped/updating transfers, and six focused RTL tests. It excludes autonomous system/storage/ROM tops and unrelated working-tree changes.
+
+Run tools/check-cpu-integration-rtl.py --bsc PATH for six fresh bounded RTL checks. Run tools/build-cpu-integration-bridges.py --bsc PATH --lighting LIGHTING_CHECKOUT to build the production CPU and matching real mainboard bridge. The Lighting checkout must contain the exact compatible RealCard Gitlink; current tested tuple uses b09117c762a36f6d25256fc3d0de3c212ada2d61. See Lighting's docs/HARDWARE-CPU-INTEGRATION.md for configured Rust execution tests. tools/prepare-cpu-integration-inputs.py deterministically generates their six guest input images from checked-in corpus sources.
+
+RTL simulation acceptance is separate from physical FPGA qualification. No board constraints or vendor place-and-route claim is made. Neither candidate is merged into main, and RealCard publication requires explicit authorization.
